[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue, *dates parse mm/dd in eu locales*, and marked
known. Read report by report, it holds three problems. Each now has a ticket of its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser closes only the first row. The other two keep coming in after the fix.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {filed} />

## The three problems

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes
  the day first. Any date with a day of 12 or less comes out with day and month swapped:
  *7 April* goes out as *4 July*. This is the bug #4471 was opened for.
- **`hint`**: tenants on `booking-v3` print `MM/DD/YYYY` under the form's date field. Their people
  type the month first, as told, and the form reads the field day first. Only reports sent
  through the form of a `booking-v3` tenant. The parser fix does not touch it.
- **`one-day`**: the date moves by one day; day and month are not swapped. It depends on where the
  reader is: *"Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday."* A date-only value is
  going through a timezone conversion. The desk listed these reports in its notes, then filed
  them under the tenant's cause.

## Why it looked like one

- Intake tags a report from the reporter's **browser**; the cause depends on the **tenant**. Every
  report from an en-US browser was tagged `hint`, wherever its tenant is.
- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line. Every subject
  here is some form of "wrong date", so three bugs went into one ticket.
- The cause table on #4471 counts the one-day moves under `parser` and `hint`, and shows `hint` as
  merged into the wrong ticket, while the page above it says one issue, one fix.

## What to do

- Track each problem on its own ticket (links in the table), not on #4471.
- Place reports by tenant and what the body shows, not by intake tag or subject.

